{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
  "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nDOUGLAS H. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER, ESQUIRE, Washington,\nD.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nCOLLEEN R. SINZDAK, Assistant to the Solicitor\nGeneral, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.;\nfor the United States, as amicus curiae,\nsupporting the Petitioner.\nG. ERIC BRUNSTAD, JR., ESQUIRE, New Haven,\nConnecticut; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MOAC Mall Holdings LLC",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER: Mr. Chief\nJustice, and may it please the Court:\nBecause of the harsh consequences of\ndesignating a procedural prerequisite\njurisdictional, this Court requires a clear\nindication from Congress before it will treat a\nlimit as such."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Transform Holdco LLC",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Transform's few appellate decisions\nconcerning an earlier rule of bankruptcy\nprocedure do not provide a clear indication of\ncon -- jurisdictional character. None of the\ncases Transform cites are from this Court, and\nnone actually designated the rule\njurisdictional. Because the requirement of a\nstay is not jurisdictional, it was subject to\nwaiver, forfeiture, and estoppel, each of which\napplies here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: In your -- I -- I\nunderstand you'd like to get to the\njurisdiction/non-jurisdiction question, but I\nthink I've almost had my fill of that. The --\ncould you just take a second to explain what\nprovision you rely on to -- as the -- to\nchallenge the lease assignment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Does your\nargument depend upon there being issues that\ncould be raised that do not go to the\nauthorization of the sale or lease? In other\nwords, I understand the argument that this\ndoesn't bar jurisdiction across the waterfront,\nbut it does seem to bar any further inquiry into\nthe validity of the sale or lease. No?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MOAC Mall Holdings LLC",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "sale of property of the estate under 363(b)\nbecause that had already happened. The sale had\nclosed. The money had been paid to Sears, and\nthere was no -- it was not subject to adjustment\nif the designated leases were later held not to\nbe eligible for assignment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: You sure?\nJUSTICE ALITO: Yeah.\nJUSTICE GORSUCH: All right. I --I\n-- I think what I'm struggling with and I'm --I\n-- I sense my colleagues are too is that it's a\nlittle unusual to say a good faith purchaser of\na bankruptcy asset might have to disgorge it,\nyou know, some years later after perhaps the\nbankruptcy estate has been eliminated and -- and\n-- and the bankruptcy's discharged.\nSo, what do we do about that? Does\nevery good faith purchaser now take an asset\nsubject to the possibility that it will be\nreverted to and a bankruptcy estate might have\nto re-emerge? I mean, I -- I'm just -- I'm just\nunfamiliar with -- I'm not a bankruptcy expert."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can -- can I ask you to make an assumption you don't want to make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, I think there might be additional relief that could be provided to --to Mall of America in terms of out of the compensation from the sale. That's not been explored yet."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the rule --the statute only precludes an -- an invalidation of the -- of the sale. Of course, we think this is an assignment, not a sale, so it doesn't apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I just wanted to ask whether in part -- partly in response to Justice Gorsuch's question, is it your view that the statute itself, (m), assuming that it applies, does contemplate circumstances in which you might have to unravel it because it's -- it -- it only talks about the validity of a sale that has been made in good faith?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Sinzdak",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 363(m) is not jurisdictional because nothing in its text suggests that it is, and there is no other evidence that satisfies the clear statement rule described in Arbaugh."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I know there's a resistance to projecting what would happen when this case -- if this case goes back, but what do you think will happen?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, I --I hear everything you say, okay? So take it as read, okay? But, normally -- I mean, my bankruptcy experience is limited, so --and yours is much, much more -- you -- you have access to people with great more expertise, and so I'm -- I'm -- I'm really pleading for that, okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we can pick either one for jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1991, Sears and MOAC entered into a 100-year freely assignable essentially rent-free ground lease. Sears built the building, not MOAC. Decades later, in 2018, when Sears filed for bankruptcy, the building that Sears built with this ground lease became property of the bankruptcy estate of Sears' bankruptcy estate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statutory remedy, the exclusive remedy is the avoidance powers. That's not available here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "explained, if you reverse a sale order on appeal, it does nothing to affect the sale. The sale cannot be overturned."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. Help me"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But you don't want that, do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, to context, boy -- jumping to context in a place where we've always said you need a clear statement in the text, where is your clear statement in 363(m)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BRUNSTAD",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: The clear statement is does not affect the validity of a sale. It's a subject matter constraint, not a procedural rule. The other statutes involve things like file your notice of appeal in 14 days or a time limit. This is not a procedural limitation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: One thing I'm confident about is -- is -- is that I -- I am -- I am deeply confused by this case. But I just want to make sure my confusion is at least what I think it is. How about that? That you would say that, right, we normally require magic words like \"no jurisdiction\"? That those are typically in personam actions in an in rem world?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Can't touch the sale if it was made in good faith?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-808b7a248319-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I -- I'm sorry, did we have a common law rule on good -- it being the good faith buyer could still challenge the sale?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1270",
      "confidence": 0.0,
